                <pb facs="0179" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00Electoral Law/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gross</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-01T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1927—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Department wishes you to telegraph present status of the electoral law and
                    whether there is any possibility of enactment of the proposed law in near
                    future, in which event you will request delay until the Department is able to
                    express its views. The Department has not approved any final draft of such a
                    law.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
